Z||000000||gkozlov||11-12-2000||10:00 AM||||Does anyone know how to set up an FTP site. I have a ton of stuff to share. Alot of it is Fiero related. I run a DSL modem so connection and speed is not a problem. If anyone knows how to or a how to page please fill me in.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">  <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||btoth||11-12-2000||11:24 AM||||Well, if you have a static IP with your DSL service you can download Microsoft's free web server software (assuming you're using windows).  (I think it may come on the Win '98 cd, not sure though.)  It's easy to set up your computer as a web server or ftp server (or both) with it.  Then just give everyone your IP address.||||reg||1
Z||000002||gkozlov||11-12-2000||11:53 AM||||You wouldn't know what its called would you?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">  <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||btoth||11-12-2000||12:45 PM||||Personal Web Server.  (Usually just called PWS).  It is on the Win '98 for sure (just found my cd).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  It's in the Add-Ons folder.  Don't know about '95.  I think to download it from Microsoft you have to download the entire IE package with the 'Internet Tools'.||||reg||7
Z||000004||JohnnyK||11-12-2000||09:59 PM||||I'd go with a program called Serv-u FTP server.. I really like it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||11-12-2000||11:32 PM||||I strongly recomend you understand all the security issues with doing this before you load software. If you don't do it right you'll end up with the whole machine open to the world. At the least you should consider some type of password protection vs. annonymous access. Annon access FTP and Web serving could also be a violation of your DSL contract.<P>ALL DSL/Cable users should make sure ALL the "critical" Win9X and IE updates are installed. These are nearly all security issues.<P>Actually speed may be an issue. many DSL/Cable connections are asymetric. The down speed from them to you often aint the same as the speed going up.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cliff Pennock||11-13-2000||04:54 AM||||I agree with Ogre here. If security is an issue, I would most certainly <B>not</B> use Microsoft's Personal Web Server. That's like hanging a sign on your PC: "Hackers Welcome". There are other more secure FTP servers out there. Try searching on <A HREF="http://www.tucows.com." TARGET=_blank>www.tucows.com.</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||gkozlov||11-13-2000||11:24 AM||||Thanks for the responces. I think im just too stupid to get this thing right. I figured setting up a FTP would easy. Ill just do some research before I start asking questions to a subject I know nothing about. Once again thank you.<P>I have tons of Games, applications, MP3 and Fiero related stuff to share. There are Fiero related downloads on my homepage and ive got more. Check out my sig for the link.<P> Oh yeah if you guy and gals know any good tutorial websires on this subject please post them. Step by step woulds be great.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">   <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A><p>[This message has been edited by gkozlov (edited 11-13-2000).]||||reg||1
